    "q-353133": {
      "dom_id": "step-q353133",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284587/assets/1a6077b85e5dd3bc54daa6eaf4c6205c631443f7a6825b5313f7f62e2776af2f.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-6,-2],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-2,2),$ and the line segment for $x\\in (2,6].$ Using the additive property of integrals, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-2].$ The corresponding region is an upper semi-circle of radius $2$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,2).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-8.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (2,6].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-10.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}-{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\pi -8-10 \\\\  & =2\\pi -18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
